BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cable Class - October
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T143000
UID:bistitchual-9624989597954@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a one session Cable Class. The class will 
 be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday October 3 from 12:30pm-2:30pm
  Have you been fantasizing about the cable sweater of your dreams? Take a 
 step towards making that dream a reality with our Cables Class and learn t
 he secrets of the deceptively simple yet hugely impactful cable knitting t
 echnique. In this class you will learn cable basics which will allow you t
 o tackle any cable project. Students will work through a small pattern tha
 t exemplifies cable techniques. Students should already be comfortable wit
 h the knit and purl stitches\, ribbing\, and pattern reading. Please bring
  worsted weight yarn and appropriate needles. If you need materials\, you 
 can purchase them in store with a 10% class discount. Cable needles will b
 e provided. Please note that classes will only proceed if we have a minimu
 m of two attendees . If the minimum is not met\, there will be the option 
 for a refund or to reschedule. There will be a four person maximum for eac
 h class. Please pre-book your spot to let us know you are coming! Cancella
 tion Policy Classes must be paid for at the time of registration to reserv
 e your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior to the start of the first
  class will be given a store credit. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs pr
 ior to the start of the class will not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/cable-class-october
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to Spin Your Own Yarn- September
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T163000
UID:bistitchual-9622755082498@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Spinning Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday September 26
 \, October 3\, and October 10 from 3:00pm-4:30pm Learn how to transform fi
 bre into yarn with our drop spindle class! In this class you will learn ho
 w to use a drop spindle to spin starting with woolly fibre and ending with
  a completed\, ready to use yarn. You will learn how to spin a single ply 
 yarn\, how to spin a 2-ply yarn using the Andean Plying method\, and how t
 o chain ply for a 3-ply yarn over three classes. We will discuss spinning 
 basics as well as different types of yarn\, fibres\, processing tools\, an
 d preparations and how these affect the finished yarn. Drop spindles must 
 be brought by students or purchased in store. 50g of fibre provided in two
  different colours. Please note that classes will only proceed if we have 
 a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum is not met\, there will be the
  option for a refund or to reschedule. There will be a four person maximum
  for each class. Please pre-book your spot to let us know you are coming! 
 Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at the time of registration t
 o reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior to the start of t
 he first class will be given a store credit. Classes cancelled less than 4
 8 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/learn-to-spn-september
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Knitting Course - September *NEW TIME*
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T153000
UID:bistitchual-9610187407618@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Knitting Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday September 13th
 \, 20th\, and 27th from 2:00-3:30pm Have you always wanted to learn to kni
 t? We’ve got you covered! Beginner Knitting is a course for brand new be
 ginners\, and over these three 1.5hr classes\, Mike will teach you everyth
 ing you need to create a basic project from beginning to end. Our class si
 ze is capped at 4 people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need
 . Mike will share lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way.
  (No experience necessary) Materials: Yarn and needles will be provided. W
 hat We’ll Learn - How to make a slip knot. - Casting on. - The Knit stit
 ch. - The Purl stitch. - Exploring Knit / Purl combinations. - Binding off
 . - Weaving in ends. - Fixing common mistakes and how to avoid them. - Com
 mon uses of flat knitting. - Intro into Ravelry. Please note that classes 
 will only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum i
 s not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. There 
 will be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot to
  let us know you are coming! About the instructor : Tired of disposing of 
 clothes that were still perfectly wearable\, Mike (he/him) started craftin
 g mainly as a means of mending and repair. This led him to knitting (and l
 ater crochet)\, which pretty much immediately became one of his favourite 
 tools of self-expression. Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at 
 the time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or mo
 re prior to the start of the first class will be given a store credit. Cla
 sses cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not b
 e reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-knitting-course-september-2-0
 0-3-30
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Crochet - September
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260920T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260920T173000
UID:bistitchual-9533060808962@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a two session Beginner Crochet Course. The
  classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday September 20th an
 d 27th from 4:00pm-5:30pm Learn the fundamentals of crochet in this two pa
 rt class. We will be covering chaining and single crochet\, as well as dou
 ble and half-double crochets. Don’t know what any of that means? Great\,
  you’re in the right place! We’ll provide all the materials\, includin
 g a simple pattern that teaches you common terms and instructions you’ll
  encounter in most crochet projects. We will also discuss how to choose th
 e appropriate yarn and hook for a project as well as where you can take yo
 ur crafting after you master these basic techniques. There’s a lot to le
 arn\, and we’re excited to accompany your beginning in the wonderful cra
 ft of crochet! Materials are included! - 50g ball of worsted weight cotton
  in your choice of colour - 6mm crochet hook Our class size is capped at 4
  people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. Mike will share
  lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. About the instru
 ctor: Tired of disposing of clothes that were still perfectly wearable\, M
 ike (he/him) started crafting mainly as a means of mending and repair. Thi
 s led him to knitting (and later crochet)\, which pretty much immediately 
 became one of his favourite tools of self-expression. Please note that cla
 sses will only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the mini
 mum is not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. T
 here will be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your sp
 ot to let us know you are coming! Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid
  for at the time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 h
 rs or more prior to the start of the first class will be given a store cre
 dit. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class wi
 ll not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-crochet-september-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
